 "_note": "v1 with: temporal_sequences dropped (its wrong options are the time slots the story mentions, so likelihood scoring sits far below chance: 0.03-0.04 at 360M/1.7B); every multiple-choice leg paired with an options-only twin (<leg>_optonly: same items and order, prompt replaced by 'Answer:') -- option prior, and for proverqa/clutrr the content-free label prior used to calibrate; proverqa joined with semforge's z3 audit (semforge-internal results/audit/proverqa.json @30563da): row field `audit` = z3_label, label_agrees, steps, claimed, mandatory, minimal_support, forced_chain (no premise set smaller than the cited chain proves it; None for neutral rows); semforge does not compute a certified depth (spine) for ProverQA, `mandatory` is the nearest proxy. GSM-Infinite is scored by greedy generation, first-line exact match (12 new tokens, no chain of thought): read it at 3B and above only. synthworlds_* are a knowledge-vs-reasoning CONTROL, not a depth probe (open answers scored by gold likelihood). MuSR with murder mysteries is the separate reasoning_depth_long_v2 (max_length 2048). KnowLogic stays: SCoRE, its hop-annotated successor, has no released data (github pokerwf/KnowLogic holds only the README). Read with reasoning_core.evaluation.depth_report: chance-adjusted accuracy per depth, context gain over the options-only twin, calibrated accuracy for closed-label legs, paired deltas."
